research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/ex-harmonic-series-diverges.md:1345:- **This is a necessary condition and never a sufficient one.** It rules a series out; it never rules one in. The harmonic series has terms tending to $0$ and diverges, which is exactly the content of [[fs-nth-term-test-converse]].
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/ex-harmonic-series-diverges.md-1346-
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/ex-harmonic-series-diverges.md-1347-- **What the proof actually uses.** Only that the partial sums converge and that consecutive partial sums differ by a term. No sign hypothesis is placed on $(a_k)$, and none is available at this point on the page.
