research/audit/wave7-preserved-refuters/thm-geometric-series--cd0838e53d925e6e.prompt.md-1249-[A1] $(s_n)$ converges to some real $S$ ([[def-series]], [[def-real-limit]]).
research/audit/wave7-preserved-refuters/thm-geometric-series--cd0838e53d925e6e.prompt.md-1250-
research/audit/wave7-preserved-refuters/thm-geometric-series--cd0838e53d925e6e.prompt.md-1251-[L1] The recursion clause of the finite sum: $s_{n+1} = s_n + a_n$ for every $n \in \mathbb{N}$ ([[def-finite-sum]], [[def-series]]).
research/audit/wave7-preserved-refuters/thm-geometric-series--cd0838e53d925e6e.prompt.md-1252-
research/audit/wave7-preserved-refuters/thm-geometric-series--cd0838e53d925e6e.prompt.md-1253-[L2] Convergence depends only on the tail: if $(x_n)$ converges to $x$ then so does its $1$-st tail $(x_{n+1})_{n}$ ([[lem-limit-of-tail]], [[def-sequence]]).
