research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6-retry27-fs-nth-term-test-converse.prompt.md-1082-1.1 The sequence $(s_{n+1})_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$ is the $1$-st tail of $(s_n)$, and it converges to $S$. [A1, L2]
